stateDiagram-v2
    direction LR
    state "scheduled" as scheduled
    state "cancelled (class)" as class_cancelled
    state "completed" as completed
    state "waiting" as waiting
    state "promoted" as promoted
    state "cancelled (waitlist)" as waitlist_cancelled
    state "none" as refund_none
    state "required" as refund_required
    state "resolved" as refund_resolved

    [*] --> scheduled: class create / store schedule
    scheduled --> class_cancelled: admin cancel / cancel live bookings and waiting entries
    scheduled --> completed: Celery end-time sweep [end_at <= now] / complete and audit
    scheduled --> completed: assigned PT confirms [start_at <= now] / complete and audit
    [*] --> waiting: join waitlist [full class, verified, queue room] / allocate position
    waiting --> promoted: cancellation or payment release [capacity opens and candidate eligible] / create pending_payment hold and notify
    waiting --> waitlist_cancelled: leave, class cancel, or ineligible promotion candidate / release queue entry
    promoted --> waiting: rejoin [eligible and full] / allocate new position
    waitlist_cancelled --> waiting: rejoin [eligible and full] / allocate new position
    refund_none --> refund_required: paid cancellation or late paid class success / flag staff review
    refund_required --> refund_resolved: admin records resolution [reason supplied] / audit resolution
    refund_resolved --> refund_none: new checkout or promotion / clear prior resolution marker

    note bottom of promoted
        Promotion creates a payment hold without a payment row.
        The promoted member starts checkout, which attaches a new pending payment.
    end note
    note bottom of refund_resolved
        Internal bookkeeping only; no provider reversal confirmation.
    end note
